          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00295:alt:fig-00004-alt",
              "text": "(1-Methylbutyl)trimethylammonium hydroxide (ball and stick also shown) reacts to form 1-pentene and 2-pentene. The more hindered, less accessible (C 2) and less hindered, more accessible (C 1) hydrogens are labeled."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_24_07_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
